1
00:00:03,711 --> 00:00:05,379
Oh, hey, if you guys are free
this weekend,

2
00:00:05,546 --> 00:00:07,172
I won a night of wine tasting from work.

3
00:00:07,590 --> 00:00:08,757
-That sounds fun.
-Mmm-hmm.

4
00:00:08,925 --> 00:00:12,136
Like, how come scientists
don't win free stuff like sales people do?

5
00:00:12,303 --> 00:00:15,431
'‘Cause we're not in it for the stuff.
(CHUCKLES) We're in it for the groupies.

6
00:00:17,934 --> 00:00:20,686
Personally, I find the notion
of external rewards demeaning.

7
00:00:20,853 --> 00:00:23,939
I pursue science
for the intrinsic joy of discovery.

8
00:00:24,607 --> 00:00:26,942
But you always say
that you wanna win a Nobel Prize.

9
00:00:27,860 --> 00:00:29,486
I also say, "Don't contradict me
in front of my friends,"

10
00:00:29,654 --> 00:00:30,696
but that you don't remember.

11
00:00:32,281 --> 00:00:33,657
All right. Well, let me know
if you guys wanna go.

12
00:00:33,824 --> 00:00:34,825
I would love to.

13
00:00:34,992 --> 00:00:37,953
I do enjoy the complexity
of an aged Pinot Noir.

14
00:00:38,120 --> 00:00:41,039
I'm sure that would pair nicely
with your five nuggets of chicken.

15
00:00:43,084 --> 00:00:45,086
Well, it sounds like a nice night.
We should go.

16
00:00:45,253 --> 00:00:47,380
Wine again? Yeah, no, thank you.

17
00:00:47,547 --> 00:00:50,466
I like my grapes the old-fashioned way,
in a juice box.

18
00:00:51,926 --> 00:00:52,968
Well, I'm going.

19
00:00:53,135 --> 00:00:54,970
You couldn't stop me
from getting a massage at the mall,

20
00:00:55,137 --> 00:00:56,471
and you're not stopping me now.

21
00:00:56,806 --> 00:01:00,309
I shouldn't have to see my girlfriend
get groped in public by another man.

22
00:01:01,561 --> 00:01:02,562
And I shouldn't have to see

23
00:01:02,728 --> 00:01:05,313
my boyfriend riding on a train
for children, around the mall.

24
00:01:07,316 --> 00:01:08,984
The little choo-choo for toddlers?

25
00:01:09,151 --> 00:01:10,986
And now you know why I needed the massage.

26
00:01:12,530 --> 00:01:13,531
Well, we're out.

27
00:01:13,698 --> 00:01:15,700
Bernie can't drink, 'cause she's pregnant.

28
00:01:15,866 --> 00:01:20,078
And she's pregnant because we had sex,
and we had sex because, well... (CHUCKLES)

29
00:01:20,246 --> 00:01:21,247
Come on.

30
00:01:23,499 --> 00:01:24,958
It's okay, you should go.

31
00:01:25,209 --> 00:01:26,710
-You sure?
-Of course.

32
00:01:26,877 --> 00:01:28,795
Yeah, give her a break from...

33
00:01:28,963 --> 00:01:30,297
Well, come on.

34
00:01:32,425 --> 00:01:34,802
Well, Bernadette, looks like
Saturday night, it's you and me.

35
00:01:35,219 --> 00:01:36,428
Me? How? Why?

36
00:01:38,097 --> 00:01:39,223
Well, it makes perfect sense.

37
00:01:39,390 --> 00:01:42,893
Look, because you're an expectant mother,
you can't drink alcohol, I don't like to.

38
00:01:43,060 --> 00:01:45,228
You can't have sushi, and I don't like to.

39
00:01:45,396 --> 00:01:46,897
You can't go in hot tubs.

40
00:01:47,064 --> 00:01:49,691
I consider them
vats of sweaty-people soup.

41
00:01:51,694 --> 00:01:53,028
Gee, Sheldon, I don't know.

42
00:01:53,195 --> 00:01:56,865
Oh, come on. Well, roller coasters,
caffeine, runny eggs.

43
00:01:57,033 --> 00:01:58,743
I've been avoiding these things
all my life.

44
00:01:58,909 --> 00:02:00,869
And now, because you're pregnant,
you have to.

45
00:02:02,163 --> 00:02:04,206
The difference is,
she's bringing life into the world,

46
00:02:04,373 --> 00:02:05,374
and you sucked it out.

47
00:02:07,752 --> 00:02:08,961
I guess we could give it a try.

48
00:02:09,587 --> 00:02:11,630
Well, little lady,
you've heard of party hardy.

49
00:02:11,797 --> 00:02:13,381
Get ready to party hardly.

50
00:02:15,718 --> 00:02:17,177
I bet you'd like a drink right now.

51
00:02:20,056 --> 00:02:22,058
(THEME SONG PLAYING)

52
00:02:46,707 --> 00:02:49,042
Hey, you think it'd be okay
if I brought Claire to the wine tasting?

53
00:02:49,210 --> 00:02:50,294
Sure, I'd like to meet her.

54
00:02:50,461 --> 00:02:52,296
Oh, that's great. I've been wanting
her to meet you guys, too.

55
00:02:52,463 --> 00:02:54,089
So, this seems
like the perfect opportunity.

56
00:02:54,590 --> 00:02:55,632
But I won't be there.

57
00:02:55,800 --> 00:02:56,884
Funny how that worked out.

58
00:02:59,428 --> 00:03:00,971
Does this mean
Emily's not in the picture anymore?

59
00:03:01,138 --> 00:03:02,180
No, I'm still dating her.

60
00:03:02,640 --> 00:03:03,724
Okay, help me out.

61
00:03:03,891 --> 00:03:06,393
How are you doing this?
Do they know about each other?

62
00:03:06,560 --> 00:03:10,313
They know that we're not exclusive,
and we just don't ask too many questions.

63
00:03:10,481 --> 00:03:13,108
You know what, it's like how I play
Warlords of Ka'a with you,

64
00:03:13,275 --> 00:03:15,902
and Elder Sign with Frank and Alicia.

65
00:03:18,239 --> 00:03:19,365
Who's Frank and Alicia?

66
00:03:20,282 --> 00:03:24,244
You and I spend a lot of time together.
Can there be a little mystery between us?

67
00:03:26,205 --> 00:03:27,915
Okay, everything's hooked up, we're ready.
(CHUCKLES)

68
00:03:28,457 --> 00:03:30,709
I am going to record this for posterity.

69
00:03:30,876 --> 00:03:32,502
All right, here goes nothing.

70
00:03:32,837 --> 00:03:33,921
"Here goes nothing"?

71
00:03:34,088 --> 00:03:35,756
This is the initial test
for our prototype.

72
00:03:35,923 --> 00:03:38,342
-Can we give it a little more gravitas?
-Fine.

73
00:03:38,968 --> 00:03:39,969
Preliminary trial

74
00:03:40,136 --> 00:03:42,763
of the infinite persistence
gyroscopic navigational system,

75
00:03:42,930 --> 00:03:44,139
phase one, commencing.

76
00:03:44,640 --> 00:03:45,849
Uh... Maybe it's your voice.

77
00:03:46,016 --> 00:03:48,143
I'm gonna see if I can get
James Earl Jones to do it in post.

78
00:03:50,354 --> 00:03:51,480
(WHIRRING)

79
00:03:52,064 --> 00:03:53,065
(CHUCKLEYS)

80
00:03:53,232 --> 00:03:54,233
(EXCLAIMS SOFTLY)

81
00:03:56,652 --> 00:03:57,653
Ah...

82
00:03:58,279 --> 00:04:00,739
It's... It's beautiful.

83
00:04:03,075 --> 00:04:04,826
Actually, it's making me dizzy.

84
00:04:05,494 --> 00:04:06,703
Good, it's not just me. (CHUCKLES)

85
00:04:13,544 --> 00:04:15,003
-CLAIRE: Hello.
-Hey, Claire.

86
00:04:15,254 --> 00:04:18,257
-Hey, what's up?
-Hi, yeah, um, I was wondering

87
00:04:18,424 --> 00:04:20,551
if you're free Saturday night. (CHUCKLES)

88
00:04:20,843 --> 00:04:22,719
All my friends
are going to a wine tasting.

89
00:04:23,345 --> 00:04:24,429
Sure.

90
00:04:24,597 --> 00:04:27,766
I guess. If you don't think
meeting your friends is too big a step.

91
00:04:28,476 --> 00:04:30,352
Why would it be too big a step?

92
00:04:30,811 --> 00:04:33,313
I don't know,
I just don't want things to get weird.

93
00:04:34,482 --> 00:04:36,442
Nothing to worry about.

94
00:04:36,650 --> 00:04:39,235
People meet people all the time,
and it isn't weird.

95
00:04:39,612 --> 00:04:40,654
I met Bon Jovi once,

96
00:04:40,821 --> 00:04:43,573
which you'd think might be weird.
Turns out, total sweetheart.

97
00:04:45,785 --> 00:04:49,455
Okay, but you and I
have been keeping things casual.

98
00:04:49,622 --> 00:04:52,333
Will you introduce me as your friend
or as your girlfriend?

99
00:04:53,042 --> 00:04:55,002
What if I like them
and they don't like me?

100
00:04:55,169 --> 00:04:57,171
What if they like me
and I don't like them?

101
00:04:58,088 --> 00:05:00,173
Boy, it wasn't this hard with Bon Jovi.

102
00:05:00,341 --> 00:05:03,093
I said, "You rock!"
He said, "Thanks, man." And that was that.

103
00:05:06,096 --> 00:05:07,889
(SCRATCHES AND SNIFFS)

104
00:05:12,561 --> 00:05:14,354
-Hey, you ready to go?
-Hang on.

105
00:05:14,605 --> 00:05:15,606
What are you doing?

106
00:05:15,856 --> 00:05:18,692
Oh, I found a scratch-and-sniff book
about wine tasting.

107
00:05:20,194 --> 00:05:22,446
It teaches
the different flavor notes to look for.

108
00:05:22,613 --> 00:05:26,241
-You actually smell the wine?
-I mostly just smell my nasal spray.

109
00:05:27,618 --> 00:05:30,370
-Are your sinuses acting up?
-Since my preschool got a bunny.

110
00:05:32,122 --> 00:05:34,082
Hey, are you still hanging out
with Bernadette tonight?

111
00:05:34,250 --> 00:05:37,920
Yes, and we're going to prove that
we don't need alcohol to enjoy ourselves.

112
00:05:38,212 --> 00:05:39,213
Oh, good for you.

113
00:05:39,380 --> 00:05:43,880
Or caffeine, tobacco, sushi, soft cheese,
processed meats and Jacuzzis,

114
00:05:44,134 --> 00:05:46,136
which can all be harmful
to an unborn baby.

115
00:05:47,263 --> 00:05:49,181
No honey-baked ham in a hot tub, got it.

116
00:05:50,266 --> 00:05:51,350
No, and no bubble baths either.

117
00:05:51,517 --> 00:05:53,268
They can increase the risk
of a urinary tract infection--

118
00:05:53,435 --> 00:05:54,436
-Okay, have fun.
-Yeah.

119
00:05:54,603 --> 00:05:57,731
Oh, and no swordfish, king mackerel,
shark or tilefish,

120
00:05:57,898 --> 00:05:58,940
which are all high in mercury.

121
00:05:59,108 --> 00:06:00,150
We're leaving now!

122
00:06:00,317 --> 00:06:02,986
And no contact with guinea pigs
or hamsters or their droppings.

123
00:06:03,153 --> 00:06:05,613
No cat litter boxes, no paint fumes--

124
00:06:05,781 --> 00:06:07,115
Okay, we're leaving. Love you, bye!

125
00:06:09,994 --> 00:06:11,412
Boy, do I love restrictions.

126
00:06:14,790 --> 00:06:17,125
-(SOFT MUSIC PLAYING)
-Hey. (CHUCKLES) Where is everybody?

127
00:06:17,334 --> 00:06:18,793
Oh, we're the first ones here.

128
00:06:19,420 --> 00:06:20,421
Oh.

129
00:06:20,796 --> 00:06:21,880
Cool.

130
00:06:22,882 --> 00:06:25,134
Yeah. (CHUCKLES) Cool.

131
00:06:28,470 --> 00:06:29,471
(SIGHS)

132
00:06:32,308 --> 00:06:35,436
Now, I don't remember the last time
it was just you and me hanging out.

133
00:06:35,603 --> 00:06:37,688
Oh, I do, it was three years ago.

134
00:06:38,314 --> 00:06:41,900
Oh, yeah, then we said
we should do it more often.

135
00:06:42,067 --> 00:06:43,943
(CHUCKLES) And... And then, here we are.

136
00:06:49,158 --> 00:06:50,159
(SIGHS)

137
00:06:52,828 --> 00:06:54,287
So, Sheldon and Bernadette
are hanging out.

138
00:06:54,872 --> 00:06:57,583
I know. What are they gonna talk about?

139
00:06:57,750 --> 00:06:58,751
(BOTH LAUGH)

140
00:06:59,251 --> 00:07:00,585
I don't know.

141
00:07:01,462 --> 00:07:03,130
I really don't know.

142
00:07:04,590 --> 00:07:05,591
Hey.

143
00:07:05,758 --> 00:07:07,009
-Oh, good!
-Oh, thank God!

144
00:07:08,218 --> 00:07:09,219
You guys been here long?

145
00:07:09,386 --> 00:07:11,012
-No, two minutes.
-But, yes.

146
00:07:13,223 --> 00:07:14,224
Where's Claire?

147
00:07:14,516 --> 00:07:15,600
Oh, she's meeting us here.

148
00:07:15,768 --> 00:07:18,771
Hey guys, do me a favor, and don't ask
too many questions about the relationship.

149
00:07:18,938 --> 00:07:20,522
We're just keeping it casual.

150
00:07:20,814 --> 00:07:24,526
Oh, so, I shouldn't ask her how she feels
about being a member of your harem?

151
00:07:26,028 --> 00:07:28,488
Yeah, I know you're teasing,
but watch out for karma.

152
00:07:29,031 --> 00:07:31,158
Hey, Penny,
isn't that your old boyfriend, Zack?

153
00:07:32,242 --> 00:07:33,326
Oh, yeah.

154
00:07:33,535 --> 00:07:35,620
-Are you gonna say hi to him?
-Uh, I don't know.

155
00:07:35,788 --> 00:07:38,457
Hey, while you decide,
who's better in bed?

156
00:07:38,624 --> 00:07:41,043
Big, hot Zack or wheezy little Leonard?

157
00:07:44,254 --> 00:07:45,588
Neener-neener.

158
00:07:48,217 --> 00:07:50,219
- I brought sparkling cider.
-Oh...

159
00:07:50,511 --> 00:07:52,763
The bubbles tickle my nose.

160
00:07:53,472 --> 00:07:56,558
I'll just open this now, so it can get
nice and flat before we drink it.

161
00:07:58,727 --> 00:07:59,728
So, what do you wanna do tonight?

162
00:07:59,937 --> 00:08:01,730
Oh, I have quite the evening planned.

163
00:08:02,022 --> 00:08:05,233
Yeah, our fetus-friendly
festival of fun begins,

164
00:08:05,442 --> 00:08:08,528
with an in-depth look
at the world of model trains.

165
00:08:08,696 --> 00:08:10,197
And then, we'll kick things up a notch,

166
00:08:10,364 --> 00:08:12,949
and explore all the different ways
that you can make toast.

167
00:08:14,576 --> 00:08:15,743
There's more than one?

168
00:08:17,079 --> 00:08:18,622
-You've heard of French toast?
-Yeah.

169
00:08:18,789 --> 00:08:19,915
-And cinnamon toast?
-Yeah.

170
00:08:20,082 --> 00:08:21,124
-Melba toast?
-Yeah.

171
00:08:21,291 --> 00:08:22,333
You get where I'm going here?

172
00:08:24,712 --> 00:08:25,754
Yeah.

173
00:08:29,383 --> 00:08:30,884
I'm getting an earthy note.

174
00:08:31,051 --> 00:08:33,094
Yeah. There's definitely some oak.

175
00:08:33,262 --> 00:08:35,055
Also, uh, cherries?

176
00:08:35,431 --> 00:08:36,473
I smell nothing.

177
00:08:38,600 --> 00:08:40,602
Really? Nothing?

178
00:08:41,145 --> 00:08:43,147
It's just a whole lot of Afrin.

179
00:08:44,982 --> 00:08:46,024
Penny?

180
00:08:46,442 --> 00:08:48,444
Oh, Zack, hi. You guys remember Zack?

181
00:08:48,610 --> 00:08:49,611
-Yeah. Hey, buddy.
-Hello.

182
00:08:49,903 --> 00:08:51,404
Hey, did you two get married?

183
00:08:51,572 --> 00:08:52,781
-Yeah. Mmm-hmm.
-We did.

184
00:08:53,198 --> 00:08:54,699
To each other?

185
00:08:56,285 --> 00:08:57,286
Yes.

186
00:08:57,703 --> 00:09:00,747
Cool. 'Cause other than
when you broke up with him and dated me,

187
00:09:00,914 --> 00:09:03,124
then broke up with me,
and then dated me one more time

188
00:09:03,292 --> 00:09:04,626
before going back to him,

189
00:09:04,793 --> 00:09:06,127
I was always rooting for you two.

190
00:09:07,421 --> 00:09:08,463
Thanks.

191
00:09:08,630 --> 00:09:11,132
So, how's the science world?
What're you guys up to?

192
00:09:12,051 --> 00:09:15,137
We've actually been working on a prototype
for a navigation system we invented.

193
00:09:15,304 --> 00:09:16,471
But we won't bore you with the detalils.

194
00:09:16,638 --> 00:09:18,765
Are you kidding? I love science.

195
00:09:18,932 --> 00:09:22,268
Einstein, Stephen Hawking,
Mike deGrasse Tyson.

196
00:09:24,271 --> 00:09:25,647
Mike deGrasse Tyson?

197
00:09:25,814 --> 00:09:29,317
Yeah, you know, the boxer who grew
a mustache and became a scientist.

198
00:09:31,153 --> 00:09:32,237
So, what's your invention?

199
00:09:32,946 --> 00:09:37,446
Well, we're using quantum vortices
to replace gyroscopes in guidance systems.

200
00:09:37,826 --> 00:09:40,912
And what's neat is that they can
maintain angular momentum indefinitely.

201
00:09:41,497 --> 00:09:44,208
Angular momentum.
I was wondering about that.

202
00:09:47,169 --> 00:09:51,131
You could put it in a satellite
or a rocket, and it'll run forever.

203
00:09:51,340 --> 00:09:52,591
Cool.

204
00:09:52,758 --> 00:09:54,843
Could it be used
for missiles and war stuff?

205
00:09:55,677 --> 00:09:58,346
Yeah, but we didn't create it for weapons.

206
00:09:58,514 --> 00:10:01,433
And I doubt the military would be
interested in our little guidance system.

207
00:10:01,642 --> 00:10:03,018
Is it better than the one they use now?

208
00:10:03,227 --> 00:10:04,519
-A lot!
-Way better!

209
00:10:06,105 --> 00:10:07,106
Huh.

210
00:10:07,898 --> 00:10:09,024
You sure you guys are smart?

211
00:10:16,698 --> 00:10:20,034
H-O gauge trains are 1:87th scale.

212
00:10:20,202 --> 00:10:22,954
N gauge are 1:160th scale.

213
00:10:23,288 --> 00:10:25,456
And that brings us to Z gauge at a

214
00:10:25,624 --> 00:10:30,124
"You could easily swallow i,
don't ask how I know," 1:220.

215
00:10:30,712 --> 00:10:32,046
I'm sorry, I have to ask.

216
00:10:32,923 --> 00:10:35,592
When I was five,
I ingested a Z gauge locomotive.

217
00:10:35,759 --> 00:10:37,177
I spent the next three days saying,

218
00:10:37,344 --> 00:10:40,513
"I think I can pass it, I think
I can pass it, I think I can pass it."

219
00:10:43,350 --> 00:10:45,393
What is it about trains
that you like so much?

220
00:10:45,561 --> 00:10:47,688
(SIGHS) Interesting question.

221
00:10:48,355 --> 00:10:52,400
When I was a child,
life was confusing and chaotic for me,

222
00:10:52,568 --> 00:10:54,152
and trains represented order.

223
00:10:54,403 --> 00:10:58,240
I could line them up,
categorize them, control them.

224
00:10:58,657 --> 00:10:59,741
I guess you could say

225
00:11:00,200 --> 00:11:03,077
that they gave me
a sense of calm in a world that didn't.

226
00:11:04,037 --> 00:11:06,080
-That's lovely, Sheldon.
-Yeah.

227
00:11:06,248 --> 00:11:07,916
Other than when they're
chugging through your bowels,

228
00:11:08,083 --> 00:11:09,250
these things are magic.

229
00:11:13,589 --> 00:11:14,673
I have to admit, I've been worried

230
00:11:14,840 --> 00:11:17,717
about the military applications
since we started talking about this.

231
00:11:17,885 --> 00:11:19,052
Me, too.

232
00:11:19,428 --> 00:11:20,470
Why didn't you say something?

233
00:11:20,721 --> 00:11:24,099
Same reason I don't talk about ass cancer,
it's not a pleasant topic.

234
00:11:25,851 --> 00:11:27,394
Hey, you can't let this stop you.

235
00:11:27,561 --> 00:11:30,772
Almost any scientific advancement
can be used for destructive purposes.

236
00:11:30,939 --> 00:11:33,232
That's true.
Even Einstein's theory of relativity

237
00:11:33,400 --> 00:11:35,860
was later applied
to the development of nuclear weapons.

238
00:11:36,028 --> 00:11:37,612
E equals MC squared.

239
00:11:37,988 --> 00:11:41,616
Yeah, "E" is energy, "M" for mass
and "C" for the speed of light.

240
00:11:41,783 --> 00:11:42,784
(CLICKS TONGUE)

241
00:11:44,578 --> 00:11:45,579
How do you know that?

242
00:11:45,787 --> 00:11:48,414
Oh, Leonard mumbles it
when he wants sex to last longer.

243
00:11:52,211 --> 00:11:53,212
Hey, Raj.

244
00:11:53,545 --> 00:11:55,672
Hey, Claire. Good, you're here.

245
00:11:55,839 --> 00:11:57,757
Guys, this is my friend, Claire.

246
00:11:57,925 --> 00:12:00,719
We're casually dating, and there's no need
for any further questions about it.

247
00:12:03,972 --> 00:12:05,723
-Would you like a glass of wine?
- I said no questions.

248
00:12:09,144 --> 00:12:10,854
SHELDON: And last but not least,

249
00:12:11,021 --> 00:12:14,149
this is one
that I like to call Star Wars Toast

250
00:12:14,316 --> 00:12:18,403
because it has a light side
and a dark side.

251
00:12:21,949 --> 00:12:24,284
All righty,
it's time for Dungeons and Dragons.

252
00:12:25,619 --> 00:12:27,996
Dungeons and Dragons,
(SIGHS) that sounds about right.

253
00:12:29,456 --> 00:12:32,834
You're going to enjoy this,
I designed it especially for you.

254
00:12:33,001 --> 00:12:34,335
Okay, but just for a little bit.

255
00:12:35,045 --> 00:12:36,546
Oh, I have a feeling that once you start,

256
00:12:36,713 --> 00:12:39,006
you're not gonna want to,
or be allowed to, stop.

257
00:12:39,967 --> 00:12:41,176
All right.

258
00:12:42,552 --> 00:12:44,095
-Ready?
-You bet.

259
00:12:45,597 --> 00:12:47,515
Your name is Bernatrix.

260
00:12:47,683 --> 00:12:52,020
You are a warrior queen.
You're strong, beautiful, and tall.

261
00:12:52,396 --> 00:12:54,606
Ooh, I like the idea of being tall.

262
00:12:55,607 --> 00:12:57,859
I think you're gonna like a lot of things
I have in store.

263
00:12:58,026 --> 00:13:00,820
For example, in this world,
only the men get pregnant.

264
00:13:00,988 --> 00:13:04,199
So, your husband is home
trying not to pee when he laughs.

265
00:13:05,742 --> 00:13:07,160
This is getting fun. What's next?

266
00:13:07,452 --> 00:13:09,704
You're parched and weary from battle.

267
00:13:09,913 --> 00:13:11,581
You stand in front of a tavern

268
00:13:11,748 --> 00:13:15,293
that serves the coldest,
most delicious ale in all the realm.

269
00:13:16,003 --> 00:13:17,462
Oh, I haven't had a drink in months.

270
00:13:18,171 --> 00:13:19,255
What do you do?

271
00:13:20,424 --> 00:13:22,759
I storm in, slam my sword down, and say,

272
00:13:22,926 --> 00:13:24,928
"Barkeep, bring me
the strongest ale you have

273
00:13:25,095 --> 00:13:26,805
"and serve it in the skull of a goblin!"

274
00:13:30,309 --> 00:13:31,518
He wan is to see ID.

275
00:13:35,856 --> 00:13:38,525
So, Claire, we've heard
so many wonderful things about you.

276
00:13:39,151 --> 00:13:40,902
Really? Like what?

277
00:13:43,530 --> 00:13:44,822
Uh, mostly Penny's heard them.

278
00:13:48,618 --> 00:13:51,162
Boy, you get some dirty looks over there
when you ask for ice.

279
00:13:53,123 --> 00:13:55,291
Zack, this is my friend, Claire.

280
00:13:55,459 --> 00:13:56,877
You're hot. You seeing anybody?

281
00:13:59,171 --> 00:14:01,256
-She's seeing me.
-Why'd you say she's your friend?

282
00:14:01,423 --> 00:14:02,424
We're just keeping it casual.

283
00:14:02,758 --> 00:14:04,634
Why is he being casual with you?
You seem great.

284
00:14:04,801 --> 00:14:06,093
I don't know. Ask him.

285
00:14:06,345 --> 00:14:08,263
Why are you being casual with her?
She seems great.

286
00:14:16,938 --> 00:14:19,190
Maybe we should take a step back.

287
00:14:19,358 --> 00:14:21,526
Take a step back?
I'm not a young man anymore.

288
00:14:23,945 --> 00:14:27,323
No, I mean re-evaluate what we're doing
with the guidance system.

289
00:14:27,866 --> 00:14:31,286
But (SCOFFS) I got a baby on the way.
I gotta make some money.

290
00:14:31,661 --> 00:14:34,955
What good is money gonna do if we
inadvertently bring about Armageddon?

291
00:14:35,123 --> 00:14:36,415
Okay, let me stop you right there.

292
00:14:36,583 --> 00:14:40,628
We absolutely know our invention
will not be used to destroy the world.

293
00:14:40,796 --> 00:14:41,797
How?

294
00:14:41,963 --> 00:14:44,423
Because no one from the future
has come back to kill us.

295
00:14:47,427 --> 00:14:50,054
-(SIGHS) Very funny.
-You got something better?

296
00:14:50,639 --> 00:14:52,349
-No, not really.
-Okay, then.

297
00:14:54,684 --> 00:14:55,976
(TOILET FLUSHES)

298
00:14:58,563 --> 00:15:00,147
How much wine did you drink?

299
00:15:00,315 --> 00:15:03,151
Not a lot, I just couldn't start
until you walked away.

300
00:15:07,489 --> 00:15:09,991
The Hell Prawn
lunges out of the hot spring.

301
00:15:10,158 --> 00:15:11,159
(DICE CLATTERS)

302
00:15:11,451 --> 00:15:14,203
You block it with your shield.
Do you attack?

303
00:15:14,454 --> 00:15:15,455
Does it have eyes?

304
00:15:15,664 --> 00:15:18,958
Yeah, three giant red ones,
and they never blink. It's unsettling.

305
00:15:20,961 --> 00:15:22,045
I stab it in the middle eye.

306
00:15:22,504 --> 00:15:23,505
(DICE CLATTERS)

307
00:15:23,672 --> 00:15:25,215
Good choice! Critical hit!

308
00:15:25,382 --> 00:15:28,093
Your sword goes through its eye,
into its tiny brain.

309
00:15:28,260 --> 00:15:30,512
With its final dying gasp, it says,

310
00:15:30,679 --> 00:15:33,890
(HIGH-PITCHED VOICE)
"You have reduced me to a pile of sushi.

311
00:15:34,766 --> 00:15:37,560
"Enjoy me with this packet of soy sauce.

312
00:15:38,645 --> 00:15:40,897
"It's low sodium. Ah..."

313
00:15:43,191 --> 00:15:44,859
Okay, I guess I should eat the Hell Prawn.

314
00:15:45,485 --> 00:15:48,237
Using your sword,
you prepare a beautiful sushi dinner.

315
00:15:48,405 --> 00:15:52,534
You slip into the hot spring, and enjoy
the warm water on your aching joints.

316
00:15:52,701 --> 00:15:56,705
As you happily close your eyes, you recall
the incredible evening you've had,

317
00:15:56,872 --> 00:15:58,874
and notice that your (DICE CLATTERS)

318
00:15:59,749 --> 00:16:02,543
feet and ankles
are smaller than they've ever been.

319
00:16:03,879 --> 00:16:04,921
The end.

320
00:16:05,547 --> 00:16:08,716
Oh. This night turned out to be
so much more fun than I thought.

321
00:16:08,884 --> 00:16:10,385
Ooh, the fun doesn't stop.

322
00:16:10,552 --> 00:16:12,303
You're still going home
with a goodie bag full of toast.

323
00:16:16,057 --> 00:16:17,391
Thank you for this.

324
00:16:17,934 --> 00:16:20,853
You know, ever since people found out
I'm having a baby,

325
00:16:21,021 --> 00:16:23,273
I feel like I became
"Pregnant Bernadette."

326
00:16:23,440 --> 00:16:25,191
It was nice
to take a little break tonight.

327
00:16:25,775 --> 00:16:27,526
I can understand that.

328
00:16:27,694 --> 00:16:29,612
From the moment
people realized I was a genius,

329
00:16:29,779 --> 00:16:31,238
I've been "Sheldon the Genius."

330
00:16:33,074 --> 00:16:35,076
Although I've never really
wanted a break from that,

331
00:16:35,243 --> 00:16:36,661
so I suppose I don't understand.

332
00:16:37,621 --> 00:16:40,665
Which is ironic ‘cause, you know, genius.
(CHUCKLES)

333
00:16:43,293 --> 00:16:45,586
-Well, thanks again.
-You're welcome.

334
00:16:45,795 --> 00:16:48,464
And any time you need a break
from being "Bernadette the Pregnant,"

335
00:16:48,632 --> 00:16:50,717
"Bernatrix the Warrior Queen"
is here waiting.

336
00:16:51,510 --> 00:16:52,761
I might just take you up on that.

337
00:16:53,428 --> 00:16:56,431
Well, now mind you, that offer's only good
until the third trimester.

338
00:16:56,598 --> 00:16:59,058
I can't risk getting amniotic fluid
on my spot.

339
00:17:02,979 --> 00:17:05,690
Hey, dude, you're killing me with Claire.

340
00:17:05,857 --> 00:17:06,858
What're you talkin' about?

341
00:17:07,192 --> 00:17:09,360
Oh, I mean, come on, look at you.

342
00:17:09,569 --> 00:17:12,446
You're classically handsome,
you've got a swimmer's body.

343
00:17:12,697 --> 00:17:14,615
Next to you, I look like me.

344
00:17:16,284 --> 00:17:18,536
Oh, man, I didn't mean to do that.

345
00:17:18,995 --> 00:17:21,372
But I do appreciate you recognizing
my swimmer's body.

346
00:17:23,124 --> 00:17:26,252
Which, incidentally, I got from playing
Marco Polo at the YMCA.

347
00:17:29,130 --> 00:17:30,422
Yeah, okay.

348
00:17:30,590 --> 00:17:34,635
Just do me a favor, and stop
talking about how great Claire is.

349
00:17:35,720 --> 00:17:37,221
Anything for you,
my little foreign friend.

350
00:17:39,391 --> 00:17:42,352
So I gotta ask,
does Raj bring around other girls?

351
00:17:44,104 --> 00:17:47,148
Uh, you know,
I'm not really around that much.

352
00:17:47,315 --> 00:17:48,691
-Amy knows much more than I do.
-(SPUTTERS)

353
00:17:50,735 --> 00:17:52,111
I don't think
you have anything to worry about.

354
00:17:52,279 --> 00:17:54,864
Raj is a terrific guy, loyal to a fault.

355
00:17:55,240 --> 00:17:57,033
Yeah, I mean, he still has an AOL address.

356
00:17:59,619 --> 00:18:00,995
I see what you're sayin'.

357
00:18:01,955 --> 00:18:02,997
She's not so great.

358
00:18:08,962 --> 00:18:11,631
Don't listen to him.
He says crazy things all the time.

359
00:18:11,798 --> 00:18:13,174
-Watch. Marco.
-Polo.

360
00:18:16,886 --> 00:18:19,722
So, uh, what are you guys talking about?

361
00:18:19,889 --> 00:18:22,933
Your friends were just telling me
about all the other girls you're dating.

362
00:18:24,269 --> 00:18:27,981
Why would you do that?
I specifically asked you not to do that.

363
00:18:28,148 --> 00:18:30,358
-We didn't.
“You just did.

364
00:18:33,528 --> 00:18:35,530
Wow. Maybe none of you guys are smart.

365
00:18:44,789 --> 00:18:46,457
-Morning.
-Morning.

366
00:18:47,292 --> 00:18:49,252
Ugh. Too much wine.

367
00:18:49,419 --> 00:18:52,755
Oh, I overdid it myself last night.
Hair of the dog.

368
00:18:55,425 --> 00:18:56,884
Hey, did you ever think about

369
00:18:57,052 --> 00:18:59,429
the military applications
for the guidance system?

370
00:18:59,721 --> 00:19:01,055
Of course.

371
00:19:01,348 --> 00:19:02,349
Does it bother you?

372
00:19:03,808 --> 00:19:05,309
No. It did at first.

373
00:19:05,477 --> 00:19:08,563
But then I talked it through
with Frank and Alicia,

374
00:19:11,733 --> 00:19:14,235
and they really helped
put things into perspective.

375
00:19:15,028 --> 00:19:16,529
Who are these people?

376
00:19:18,239 --> 00:19:19,406
Leonard.

377
00:19:19,574 --> 00:19:21,242
Friends are like toilet paper.

378
00:19:22,869 --> 00:19:24,579
It's good to have extras under the sink.

379
00:19:58,363 --> 00:19:59,364
English - SDH

